# Files that get exec'd inside the Linux Paperless container must keep
# LF line endings regardless of the developer's git autocrlf setting,
# otherwise the shebang gets a trailing \r and Linux exec returns
# "Exec format error" on first ingestion.
scripts/post_consume_hook.py text eol=lf

# Apply LF to all Python and shell sources for consistency — most tooling
# (linters, OCR pipelines, etc.) assumes LF and a stray CRLF can fail in
# subtle ways inside containers.
*.py text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Markdown stays text but lets git pick the platform-native ending so
# Windows editors don't fight diffs on every save.
*.md text

# Binary fixtures (PDFs, images, the SQLite test DBs that live under
# tests/fixtures/) must not be touched by line-ending or whitespace
# normalization. Without this, autocrlf on Windows would corrupt them
# on a fresh clone.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.zip binary
